{"answer":"There are 7 subsets: {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}, {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}. For example, {1,8} has sum 9. Exhaustiveness follows because a valid subset cannot have one element (9 is absent) or four or more elements (the least four distinct positive elements sum to 10); the complete two- and three-element cases are enumerated below.","approaches":[{"description":"Classify a subset summing to 9 by its cardinality, then enumerate increasing tuples for the only possible cardinalities 2 and 3.","id":"cardinality-casework","outcome":"candidate","reason":"This gives a finite exhaustive classification without relying on computation."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"question_premise","basis_reference":"The question specifies the set {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} and target sum 9.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"given-universe","kind":"assumption","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The task concerns subsets of {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} whose elements sum to 9.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by steps size-bounds, pairs, and triples.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["given-universe"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"count-seven","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Exactly 7 subsets have sum 9: {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}, {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}.","step_ids":["size-bounds","pairs","triples"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"size-bounds","justification":"A one-element subset would have to be {9}, but 9 is not in the given set. Any subset with at least four elements has sum at least 1+2+3+4=10. Thus only sizes 2 and 3 can occur.","statement":"Any subset of the given set with sum 9 has either two or three elements."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["size-bounds"],"id":"pairs","justification":"Writing a two-element subset as {a,b} with a<b, the equation a+b=9 yields a=1,2,3,4, and respectively b=8,7,6,5. These are all admissible and no other a satisfies a<b.","statement":"The two-element subsets summing to 9 are exactly {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, and {4,5}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["size-bounds"],"id":"triples","justification":"Write a three-element subset as {a,b,c} with a<b<c. If a=1, then b+c=8 and b<c gives b=2 or 3, yielding {1,2,6} and {1,3,5}. If a=2, then b+c=7, b>=3, and b<c force b=3, yielding {2,3,4}. If a>=3, then a+b+c>=3+4+5=12, impossible. Hence this list is complete.","statement":"The three-element subsets summing to 9 are exactly {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
